              "textToSpeech": "According to the Canadian Food Inspection Agency, the following eligible bacterial species are probiotics that naturally form part of the gut flora, and contribute to healthy gut flora. Bifidobacterium species, including bifidobacterium adolescentis, animalis animalis, bifidum, breve, lactis, longum infantis, and longum longum. as well as, Lactobacillus species, including Lactobacillus acidophilus, casei, fermentum, gasseri, johnsonii, paracasei, plantarum, rhamnosus, and salivarius.",
